course: dictionary
lesson: 3749
title: Fluffy and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. «A fluffy chick ran to its mum.» Here fluffy means soft and covered in fine feathers. Ask what the words around it are about: chick and mum are animals, so the soft, feathery meaning fits.
explain: «The clouds were light and fluffy, like cotton wool.» Fluffy can also mean light and full of air, like fluffy pancakes or fluffy eggs. Try the meaning in the sentence: a cloud is not covered in fur, but it can be light and airy, so this meaning works.
explain: Sometimes fluffy means not serious or not important. Fluffy writing is light and chatty, and it avoids big or serious matters. Writers use this meaning in informal writing, so look for clues such as jokes or a casual tone.
explain: Fluffy is an adjective, so it describes a noun, and it changes to fluffier and fluffiest when you compare things. If the context does not settle which meaning is meant, check a dictionary.
fact: Fluffy means soft, light and covered with fur, feathers or fine hairs.
fact: Fluffy can also mean light and full of air, as in fluffy clouds or fluffy pancakes.
fact: Fluffy can mean not serious or not important, especially in informal writing.
fact: Fluffy changes to fluffier and fluffiest when you compare things.
fact: Fluffy materials such as wool trap air, which helps keep things warm, so they are good insulators.
exercise: «A fluffy chick ran to its mum.» What does fluffy mean here? | Not serious or important | Wet and muddy | *Soft and covered in fine feathers | Full of air, like a pancake
exercise: «Her essay was fluffy, full of jokes and no real facts.» What does fluffy mean here? | Warm and cosy by the fire | *Not serious or not important | Light and full of air | Soft and covered in fur
exercise: Which is the correct word to compare two clouds? | fluffyer | fluffiest | more fluffyest | *fluffier
test: «The fluffy towel dried me quickly.» What does fluffy mean here? | Made of metal | *Soft, with a thick covering like fur | Not important | Hot from the sun
test: «The fluffy clouds drifted over the hill.» What does fluffy mean here? | *Light and full of air | Dangerous | Serious and grave | Covered in fur
exam: Which sentence uses fluffy to mean not serious or not important? | *«Her fluffy writing made jokes about the weather.» | «The fluffy chick ran to its mum.» | «The fluffy clouds drifted over the hill.» | «The fluffy slipper sat by the bed.»
